{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder","id":1169822,"title":"Inspiration for Nephandi and Marauder","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-22T21:32:17-08:00","id":1169822,"title":"Inspiration for Nephandi and Marauder","content":"my players are asking for good examples of nephandi and marauders on videogames, tv, movies , books etc... any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T21:52:29-08:00","id":1169824,"title":"","content":"Not from fiction, but I think GG Allin was To Mega Therion (The Great Beast) and the perfect example of the nihilistic extremes of the 20th century. Also, Sid Vicious. If you research their biographies you'll have lots of material.<br /> <br /> From the movies, I'd say Anton Chigurh (No Country for Old Men). Also, Colonel Walter E. Kurtz (Apocalypse Now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T03:27:08-08:00","id":1169870,"title":"","content":"The crazy wizard that starts his own death cult in Lord of Illusions is a good example of a nephandus mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T03:54:59-08:00","id":1169874,"title":"","content":"Nephandi <br /> <br /> The villain in 13 Assassins, deliciously Nephandus. <br /> <br /> Anakin Skywalker in Episodes 1,2 &amp; 3. Seriously take what you know of the character from the end of ROTS and go back and watch the Anakin scenes again, pay careful heed to what he says and you realise from day 1 it's actually all about his power, his order, his justice HIS EMPIRE. <br /> <br /> Mrs Mouse from Don Bluth's animated film of Thumbalina. Terrifying stuff when you look at it, especially her signature scene. <br /> <br /> King Haggard in the Last Unicorn<br /> <br /> Omadon in Flight of Dragons for a very simplistic, unsubtle yet still beautifully done Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Melko and Sauron in the Silmarillion also Faenor in the same. Also Saruman in many respects in Lord of the Rings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T04:04:58-08:00","id":1169876,"title":"","content":"Marauders<br /> <br /> Batman and the Joker<br /> <br /> Achilles, both the classical literary work and the way the portray him in Troy. <br /> <br /> Jack the ripper as portrayed in a lot of literature <br /> <br /> Sherlock Holmes and Moriarty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T08:01:44-08:00","id":1169920,"title":"","content":"The Caveman's Valentine (2001)<br /> The Fisher King (1991)<br /> Fight Club (1999)<br /> Shutter Island (2010)<br /> Misery (1990)<br /> Secret WIndow (2004)<br /> Split (2016)<br /> American Psycho (2000)<br /> No Country for Old Men (2007)<br /> Hard Candy (2005)<br /> Red Dragon (2002)<br /> Apocalypse Now (1979)<br /> Girl, Interrupted (1999)<br /> The Collector (2009)<br /> Saw (2004)<br /> Event Horizon (1997)<br /> Hellraiser (1987)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T10:47:11-08:00","id":1169952,"title":"","content":"any examples in videogames for marauders or nephandi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T12:05:45-08:00","id":1169967,"title":"","content":"Corypheus from Dragon Age: Inquisition<br /> Shao Khan and Shang Tsung (among others) from Mortal Kombat<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T09:40:14-08:00","id":1172017,"title":"","content":"The Man in Black from the Dark Tower (both the books and the movie) is a Euthanatos-turned-Nephandus. The book version could also draw upon other Traditions instead, though, including Hollow One; the film version, though, is clearly a Euthanatos (though one with Force magic as well)<br /> <br /> One could make the argument that Balder from Bayonetta is a Chorister-turned-Nephandus as well, and Loptr was also a Nephandus as well (possibly without a tradition at all).<br /> <br /> Goku Black and Zamasu from Dragon Ball Super are arguably Nephandi as well. Goku Black was a Dual Tradition Akashic and Euthanatos. Zamasu could be seen as a mix of Euthanatos, Akashic, Wu Lung, or Chorister as well, depending on how you view the Celestial structure (admittedly, they also are better examples of Exalted characters, but the viewpoints are the same, and Mage is probably the closest WoD game to reflecting their abilities). As a point of order, Beerus is clearly NOT a Nephandus - though a God of Destruction, he is not in it to destroy all reality for the HFIL of it, but rather as a sacred duty; he's bad at it, and jokes to the contrary, but he is a pure Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> Marauders are trickier. However, Scarlet Witch in House of M is an example of a more directed Marauder, I think - the entire world is inside her creation of influence when she snaps. Legion also may be an example of one (especially in the Age of X storyline).<br /> <br /> A rare heroic example could be the heroes from &quot;Hikonin Sentai Akibaranger.&quot; Each of them is part of a shared delusion that gives them the power to turn into Sentai/rangers, but at the price of increasing disconnect to the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T07:34:12-08:00","id":1172251,"title":"","content":"Chara from Undertale<br /> They want the complete destruction of the world, and you don\u2019t meet them until alread after their plans are irreversibly complete. By which point they have pretty much won since either the game is unplayable, or they take ownership of your soul to get what they want after you try to undo it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T17:38:56-08:00","id":1172459,"title":"","content":"If we're talking Marauders, Loma Shade from the comic series <i>Shade The Changing Girl</i> is a solid contender. A bird alien who stole the Madness Coat from the earlier Shade The Changing Man, she used its powers of Madness to astral project into the body of a comatose Earth girl. She then proceeds to try to live on this blue marble, while dealing with the culture shock (both between Loma's alien culture AND her skewed understanding of Earth culture culled from out-of-date broadcasts), the fallout of her host body's former actions, and her generally tenuous grasp of Reality. The Madness Coat altering her perceptions of the world around her...or else literally shifting the world to match her thoughts and feelings.<br /> <br /> It's a heady comic, is what I'm saying. Meaning it's perfect inspiration for Mage.<br /> <br /> As you can probably tell, Loma Shade could easily be ported over to a Mage game with very little modification. Make it so her being an alien is one of her delusions, and the Madness Coat being some kind of Instrument/Wonder, and you're golden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T22:02:41-08:00","id":1172538,"title":"","content":"most of my players play League of Legends. i do not.<br /> <br /> any good examples of marauders/nephandi characters within the lore?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T10:51:22-08:00","id":1173262,"title":"","content":"ALso, was tlaking to some players...would Voldemort be a nephandi? or just &quot;A Guy&quot; with arete","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T11:33:44-08:00","id":1173268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1172538#post1172538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most of my players play League of Legends. i do not.<br /> <br /> any good examples of marauders/nephandi characters within the lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple.<br /> <br /> There's Malzahar, which is basically the herald of the eldritch abominations of the setting and trying to open a door to our world and let them all in. Stereotypical Nephandi script. Also Karthus, a mage who sacrificed himself in order to return as undead and promotes Oblivion and death for everyone. Lissandra, a sorceress empowered by frozen entities of ice and death and wants to conquer the world for them might also work.<br /> <br /> As for Marauders, I'd say Viktor, which is a guy trying to turn everyone (in a fantasy setting) into machines in order to purge them from the weakness of flesh.<br /> <br /> Plenty of other mages and assorted creatures, but I'd say the easier ones to translate as Marauders/Nephandi are these ones.<br /> <br /> League has only recently invested tons of resources to the development of its lore, which is <i>really </i>great as you ask me (they're doing an awesome job), but this also means plenty of stuff in there is still on the thin side of things when it comes to depth. Which served the purpose of the game but it's not gonna give you lots to work with<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T14:27:56-08:00","id":1173328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1173262#post1173262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ALso, was tlaking to some players...would Voldemort be a nephandi? or just &quot;A Guy&quot; with arete</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say he's just an evil wizard. He's ambitious, power hungry, racist against Muggles (read: Sleepers), and has a mortal fear of death. Granted, he's certainly willing to affect the guise of a Dark Lord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T17:48:55-08:00","id":1173382,"title":"","content":"Voldemort is indeed just an evil Mage with a stack of Jhor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:06:50-08:00","id":1174329,"title":"","content":"I don't know, he horribly maims his own soul with forbidden magic in the pursuit of power and eternal life. That's pretty distinctively a Nephandic trope, particularly for a setting where there don't appear to be evil otherdimensional entities to which one might sell one's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T15:32:47-08:00","id":1174372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1174329#post1174329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, he horribly maims his own soul with forbidden magic in the pursuit of power and eternal life. That's pretty distinctively a Nephandic trope, particularly for a setting where there don't appear to be evil otherdimensional entities to which one might sell one's soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that most Nephandi don't really care for eternal life, nor for command and control. All they seek is the ultimate end of all things. Either to appease their dark one masters, out of genuine hatred of the world, or for the sheer pleasure of watching the world burn slowly. They have nothing to lose, because even their death is in some small way a victory. Their passage through the cauls ensures their dark work will continue in another life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:03:51-08:00","id":1174377,"title":"","content":"Aye, Voldemort cannot conceive of his own mortality plus he wants to create a society of wizardry that will endure under his rule for the eternal life he has forged for himself. His whole Mudblood fascism is built around his self hatred for his own mixed blood heritage and a mistaken belief that Purebloods are totally superior in all magical ways to mudbloods. He wants a more powerful magical society that he can rule forever and bind themselves to him. While indeed evil in intent it is not nephandic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T08:37:53-08:00","id":1174559,"title":"","content":"Final Fantasy has a couple of villains that are good inspiration for Nephandi, Sephiroth has the corrupted from birth elements of a Widderslainte and the way he claims to serve Jenova but actually controls her is also very nephandic.<br /> <br /> That said, for my money the most Nephandic Final Fantasy character is Kefka Palazzo. Not only does he revel in destruction for its own sake, he only seems to be able to enjoy it if people actually die. Moreover as he grows in power he becomes obsessed that proving that life and dreams are meaningless. It is implied that the only reason he doesn't outright annihilate your party (and the world for that matter) is that it isn't enough for everyone to die, they have to die in despair. As a capstone, one of his stated goals is destroying the very bonds of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T10:23:44-08:00","id":1175212,"title":"","content":"I think the Witches from <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica </i>are a great, and horrific, example of a Marauder and their reality bubbles<i>. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T10:37:15-08:00","id":1175216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1175212#post1175212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Witches from <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica </i>are a great, and horrific, example of a Marauder and their reality bubbles<i>. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I concur wholly. The way I see it, a magical girl in Madoka Magica is a mage (complete with Phylactery) that was Awakened - and woefully misinformed - by spirits. This misinformation includes that using magick causes &quot;curses and despair&quot; or whatever to collect in their soul gems, requiring frequent purges (in a manner that suits the interests of their spirit patrons). This primes the magical girls to trend towards Quiet when they incur Paradox backlashes, disproportionately to other varieties. Ultimately resulting in a magical girl tipping into full blown Marauderdom if their Quiet is allowed to grow too great. If they ever learned that their spirit patrons were actively lying to them (because OF COURSE a liar would claim to have never lied; duh), they might start having different kinds of Paradox manifestations. Until then, though, they'll most likely turn to despair-induced madness before too long, especially since they don't know NOT to use Vulgar magick.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I'd run Madoka Magica within the context of MtAs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T11:01:14-08:00","id":1175508,"title":"","content":"I been thinking. my players might have to enter a Laberyth to save one of the players from being turned into a barrabi. they still can't understand the Scope of how dangerous a laberyth is..any recommendations on depictions of a Laberyth ?<br /> <br /> Also, our Son of Aether wants to explore the Laberyth and take elements for his own personal paradigm (to evolve humanity far beyond what its concieable)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T11:30:56-08:00","id":1175517,"title":"","content":"Also, would Sutter Cane (in the mouth of madness) be a nephandi? im analyzing John Carpenter's Apocalypse Trilogy to find more marauder/nephandi homages","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T22:29:07-08:00","id":1175695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1175517#post1175517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, would Sutter Cane (in the mouth of madness) be a nephandi? im analyzing John Carpenter's Apocalypse Trilogy to find more marauder/nephandi homages</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, very much so (at least in terms of concept and motivation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T01:04:51-08:00","id":1175711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1175508#post1175508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I been thinking. my players might have to enter a Laberyth to save one of the players from being turned into a barrabi. they still can't understand the Scope of how dangerous a laberyth is..any recommendations on depictions of a Laberyth ?<br /> <br /> Also, our Son of Aether wants to explore the Laberyth and take elements for his own personal paradigm (to evolve humanity far beyond what its concieable)</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the revised book of madness for details on the labyrinths of the nephandi.<br /> <br /> One important thing you should note is that the process of turning into a barrabus MUST be voluntary. No nephandi can force one to turn, the final decision is the mage themselves. to enter the cauls unwillingly leads only to death.<br /> <br /> Most labyrinths lie in a pocket dimension of the umbra and thus have their own rules, perhaps magic only works if it\u2019s done with intent to harm someone. Perhaps all magic requires a sacrifice of some sort, or perhaps you must scream the name of demons, or maybe all magic is easier but more severe, harder to control for the uninitiated.<br /> <br /> The labyrinth itself is dark and difficult to navigate. They are designed to make it hard for intruders to get anywhere, while the denizens have three reign to go as they please. There are traps, guardians, dead ends, and monsters around every turn, and depending on who is in charge, may have more than one than the other.<br /> A nephandus Mind mage may for example fill their labyrinth with illusions, false doors, floors that cover pits of spikes, or even more insidious things like lost loved ones, or the way home. While a Life nephandus might make all who enter feel an unquenchable hunger, which may cause intruders to become cannibalistic. And infernalist could model their labyrinth on the circles of hell with horrible sin spawn to guard each layer, while a Malfean May design their labyrinth to become more and more corrupt, disgusting, and generally unbearable the deeper you go.<br /> The threat of being ambushed by a nephandus while in their home should be ever present, and if they are particularly good at searching, they might stumble into the barracks, or altars, meeting rooms, etc. Rooms designed to be used rather than to confuse.<br /> <br /> Not all labyrinths are complicated maze like monstrosities, some can be hidden in plain site. Silent Hill would be a really good example of a labyrinth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-13-2018, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T11:26:18-08:00","id":1175806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1175508#post1175508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I been thinking. my players might have to enter a Laberyth to save one of the players from being turned into a barrabi. they still can't understand the Scope of how dangerous a laberyth is..any recommendations on depictions of a Laberyth ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Nightmare on Elm Street (1984)<br /> Aliens (1986)<br /> Big Trouble in Little China (1986)<br /> House (1986)<br /> The People Under the Stairs (1991)<br /> Event Horizon (1997)<br /> House on Haunted Hill (1999)<br /> Rose Red (2002)<br /> House of 1000 Corpses (2003)<br /> Hellboy (2004)<br /> The Cabin in the Woods (2012)<br /> Crimson Peak (2015)<br /> <br /> Also, William Hope Hodgson's The House on the Borderlands (DC/Vertigo comics did a pretty impressive graphic adaption if it in 2000 if you can find it)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T13:55:44-08:00","id":1175838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1175711#post1175711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most labyrinths lie in a pocket dimension of the umbra and thus have their own rules, perhaps magic only works if it\u2019s done with intent to harm someone. Perhaps all magic requires a sacrifice of some sort, or perhaps you must scream the name of demons, or maybe all magic is easier but more severe, harder to control for the uninitiated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't make it so NO magick works if it doesn't conform to a Fallen's vision. I would DEFINITELY make it a Realm where only Nephandic magick is <i>Coincidental</i>. That's entirely reasonable, just as it's entirely reasonable for a Hermetic Realm to see Hermetic magick Coincidental and all others as Vulgar.<br /> <br /> Make it so the players understand that a Labyrinth is the domain of the Fallen, where Nephandi have a home-field advantage. If the PCs can't or won't debase themselves in some way, they'll suffer for their purity, in that place of absolute corruption. The 'Dox backlashes should reflect the vile darkness of the Labyrinth, too. Hands that erupt from walls to claw and grasp. Oppressive, choking darkness. Weeping blood from every orifice. Even making like Silent Hill (as Saikou said), and strike the PCs with a Quiet that makes other people &quot;look like monsters&quot; to them.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, their foes don't need to worry a bit about Paradox, and can really cut loose with the monstrous transformations, withering hexes, and blasphemous summonings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T18:17:09-08:00","id":1175880,"title":"","content":"Other recommendations for Labyrinth ideas: the portion of <i>What Dreams May Come</i> that's set in Hell, <i>Beyond Bedlam/Nightscare </i>for a slow burn, H. P. Lovecraft's <i>From Beyond</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T23:43:37-08:00","id":1175924,"title":"","content":"I think the Major from hellsing ultimate is a good reference for a nephandus' personality. Look up his ten minute speech on how much he loves war. Trigger Warning: he's a former nazi that long since passed the nazis in both insanity and evil.<br /> <br /> I also think Azuma Genkaku from Deadman wonderland would make a good akashayana barrabus. He was originally buddhist, and got sick of the world. He even once said something to the effect of &quot;By brutally murdering these people, I've brought them the ultimate peace and harmony.&quot; He also seems to view his sadistic brand of nihilism as a superior form of buddhism.(he calls himself an &quot;ultra buddhist&quot; and an &quot;uber monk&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","user":"Dragonchild","date":". 01-14-2018, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T09:49:11-08:00","id":1176985,"title":"","content":"I know we have a unspoken rule of &quot;Too Soon.&quot; Buuut.<br /> <br /> I was watching a documentary on the Slenderman and the Attempt of murder related to the case. Two girls tried to kill another by claiming that they were doing a sacrifice for the Slenderman, who would take them to live in the Creepypasta mansion, becoming the servants of the Slenderman <br /> <br /> Reality can be horrible, we know..<br /> But, if we were translating this event into MtAs events, would it be considered as a nephandi initiation rite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T18:26:03-08:00","id":1177114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1169822-inspiration-for-nephandi-and-marauder?p=1176985#post1176985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know we have a unspoken rule of &quot;Too Soon.&quot; Buuut.<br /> <br /> I was watching a documentary on the Slenderman and the Attempt of murder related to the case. Two girls tried to kill another by claiming that they were doing a sacrifice for the Slenderman, who would take them to live in the Creepypasta mansion, becoming the servants of the Slenderman<br /> <br /> Reality can be horrible, we know..<br /> But, if we were translating this event into MtAs events, would it be considered as a nephandi initiation rite?</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, What the hell is wrong with people!?<br /> <br /> But anyway. The true nephandi initiation will always be the cauls, passing it and having your avatar inverted. But I can so see a bunch of nephandi who see some &quot;wannabe&quot; dark mages and tricking them into doing terrible things like that to further some other kind of plan, or just for the hell of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://fo